# Implementation Plan - Final Restoration Stabilization

I have identified the "Hidden Error" that prevented the previous fix from working. The 114MB restoration failed because our rewriter was splitting lines in the middle, occasionally missing critical `public.` references. Additionally, a technical bug in how we captured errors was hiding the true cause from us.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Line-Buffered Rewriting:** I will move to a line-by-line processing model. This ensures that every single instance of `public.` is caught and re-routed to `staging`, even if it occurs at the boundary of a data chunk.

## Proposed Changes

---

### [Component] Restoration Service
#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- **Line-Buffered Streaming**: refactor the logic to read and rewrite line-by-line. This is safer for massive SQL dumps and ensures regex/string replacements are deterministic.
- **Fix Diagnostic Masking**: Correct the `subprocess` logic to ensure that if `psql` fails, we get the **Actual SQL Error** from the database instead of a generic "I/O Error" in Python.
- **Aggressive Command Stripping**: I will extend the filter list to include `SET default_table_access_method`, `SET xmloption`, and other production-only commands that often cause permission failures in staging environments.

